course: dictionary
lesson: 13001
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Extend is a good example.
explain: «The fence extends along the whole field.» Here extend means reach or stretch from one point to another. «The library extended its opening hours.» Here it means made longer. The sentence tells you which meaning to pick.
explain: «She extended a warm welcome to the new pupil.» Here extend means offer, like holding out a hand. Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Extend means to make something longer, bigger or last longer.
fact: Extend can also mean to reach or stretch from one point to another.
fact: To extend your hand, an invitation or thanks means to offer it.
fact: «Extend a deadline» means move the deadline to a later time.
fact: In maths, «extend by 3» means add 3.
exercise: «The road extends from the school to the park.» What does extend mean here? | Closes the road | Turns the road into a path | *Reaches or stretches from one point to another | Makes the road smaller
exercise: In maths, «extend the pattern by two more shapes.» What does extend mean? | Draw a circle round the pattern | Take away the shapes | *Add more to make it longer | Colour the shapes in
exercise: «The teacher extended the deadline for the project.» What did the teacher do? | Gave the project to another class | Made the project shorter | *Moved the deadline to a later time | Cancelled the project
test: Nadia says extend only means get bigger. What is wrong with her idea? | Nothing, she is right | *It can also mean to offer something, like a welcome or a hand | It means to shrink, the opposite of bigger | It means to be happy
test: In «an extended family», what does extended mean? | Cut short | Lost | Very quiet | *Including more relatives, like aunts, uncles and cousins
exam: «The shop extended its opening hours to nine o'clock.» What does extended mean here? | Painted red | *Made longer, so the shop stayed open later | Closed early | Made smaller
